   File.WriteAllText(Path.Combine(Folder,"README.txt"),"KDA driving telemetry schema 10\nvehicle.csv and wheels.csv share sample/time keys. One sample per physics FixedUpdate after SC and recovery actuation; wheel contact/force data is the latest available native state and can lag the issued command by a step. dt_ut reports actual elapsed game time. World coordinates are KSP world axes; local x=right, y=forward, z=down. Yaw is rad/s about vehicle up; slip is atan2(lateral,forward) in degrees. Native wheel forces/torques are recorded verbatim; body mass is tonnes, aero force is N. Do not assume native wheel force units without checking its API.\nsetup.cfg includes part configs (imported torque/boost/ratios/aero and tire definitions) and all current KSP module fields. settings.csv records initial fields then changes at 1 Hz; SC flight settings also appear every vehicle sample. events.csv contains markers and stop reasons. Active driveline columns describe available imported hardware and pre-TCS torque allocation, not extra power. Reverse/airborne recovery disable vector yaw requests. Imported AWD Drift can request bounded yaw from the progressive less-countersteer input; neutral keys do not ask the axle to straighten the drift. Its active center uses a rear torque floor bounded by exported bias limits. Center/traction bias remain hardware-gated. Schema 8 adds AWD-only powered cornering trim for Race and derived Sport/Road profiles. The yaw target remains the original mode budget: trim responds to its shortfall without accumulating an integrator. It is disabled during lift, brakes, handbrake, wheel loss and slide recovery. Existing Road/Sport throttle and TCS profiles remain in force. awd_cornering_steer is normalized additional steering; yaw_deficit is rad/s; support is 0..1; rear_assist is an additional rear torque-share request only used by an imported active center. powered_rear_minimum is requested before source bias clamping. Missing wheel readings are omitted for that sample, not replaced with zero. summary.txt reports writer errors and dropped packets.\nSchemas 6, 7 and 8 append diagnostics without moving existing columns. com_local_* is actual vessel.CoM in body axes, metres. Contact points/normals are native observations, not new raycasts. ground_reference_valid and grounded_wheels identify the mean currently grounded contact plane; no road height or road-relative angles are reported while fully airborne. One/two-wheel reference planes are approximate. Ground height is perpendicular to the mean contact normal; height_gravity uses radial up. Body-local COM calculations subtract world positions before rotating to reduce float precision loss. signed_roll_* is positive right-side-down, signed_pitch_* positive nose-up; roll/pitch rates are actual angular velocity projections in deg/s, not derivatives of a changing contact plane. Legacy roll_ground_deg remains unsigned total tilt. Static geometry/CG alone does not predict a dynamic rollover.\nparts.csv samples native part mass components, crew count, resource amounts and rigidbody properties at recording start then 1 Hz. Native part.mass already includes KSP mass adjustments; prefab/crew/module/inventory components are diagnostic and must not all be added again. Optional native crew/module/inventory components are read without modifying KSP fields and left blank if unavailable. Rigidbody IDs identify shared bodies; do not sum repeated rigidbody masses. Inertia is each rigidbody principal tensor in native tonnes m2 with its principal-axis rotation, not an assembled vehicle inertia tensor. setup.cfg includes the same initial mass observations and crew names.\nSchema 9 replaces the old body-force bar with bounded native spring preload coupling. antiroll_request/cap/capped/applied_observed are requested elastic spring preload in native kN, not measured tire force. Read actual tire load from load; one-contact/bump-stop conditions can differ from requested preload. bar_preload_m is imposed spring reference displacement, physical_compression_m removes the previous bar displacement to prevent feedback; supported_mass_t updates from current vessel mass and CG. Both airborne resets the bar. The force cap is 25% travel times the softer spring rate. Seats and seated crew have zero vehicle mass through scoped Harmony patches; EVA Kerbals retain stock mass. CG calibration status/reference is in KDAImportedMass setup fields. antiroll_request/cap/capped/applied_observed are native kN; owner ID identifies the one left-wheel actuator for an axle. Right rows mirror the owner observation with opposite signed force. bar_sample_age_s must be zero (within float tolerance) for a current-step observation. A blank request/cap means the actuator never reached force calculation due to a gate; the applied observed force is zero when blocked, not a fabricated uncapped request. The original antiroll_force column is retained for compatibility but can be cleared by per-wheel update order; use antiroll_applied_observed instead. Forces can refer to contact state from the previous native step.\nSchema 7 adds rear_driveline_coupling (0 = open rear path, 1 = coupled), awd_rotation_intent, awd_added_steering, active_yaw_target_rad_s and drift_rear_minimum. Imported AWD handbrake opens the rear drive path: rear drive and engine drag are removed, engine-coupling RPM/load follow the front wheels, and the path reconnects progressively after release. Front drive remains available; this is a KDA virtual rear-coupling feature, not a claim that the source export supplies this clutch. RWD/FWD retain their existing behavior.\nCSV writes are queued on a background thread; no new forces, raycasts or controller tuning are introduced. Schema 10 adds suspension.csv: true stroke corrected for the moved collider reference, travel fraction, remaining bump/droop, target and estimated static sag, base/effective spring rate, bump-stop model force (kN), damping (kN s/m), contact speed, airtime, landing speed and bottoming episode counters, wheel arc offset and approximate proper body acceleration in g. Raw wheels.csv contactDepth/suspensionCompression are native VP diagnostics and omit the adjustable collider-center reference; use suspension.csv for kit stroke.\nRecording stops on vessel change, packing, part-count change, scene exit or shutdown.\n");
